[Music]  malcolm in the middle star frankie munez  grew up in front of audiences  from his hit show to his starring roles  in agent cody banks and big fat liar  he's kept a low profile  sense so here's what munez has been up  to since saying goodbye  to playing malcolm after the final  episode of malcolm in the middle aired  in 2006  fans were eager to find out what muniz  would do next but he needed a change of  pace  even before going to hollywood muniz was  active in theater which was how he  eventually transitioned into appearing  in commercials and landing his first  film roles  muniz had been playing malcolm for six  years and he was ready for some time  away from the camera  muniz once said that by the time his run  as malcolm was over he had quote  done little else but work for 12 years  that kind of schedule  would be difficult enough for an adult  actor to handle let alone a child actor  he didn't leave hollywood all together  but significantly cut back on his  schedule  mostly making one-off appearances on tv  shows or movies  after shooting agent cody banks 2 in  2004  muniz began to think about landing more  mature roles  but he admitted that dealing with the  transition was challenging  in an interview with about the actor  commented that he assumed that upon  becoming a legal adult  he'd begin getting more mature roles but  that wasn't the case  saying i haven't been scared but i've  really been thinking about it a lot  that i really have to do something at  this point right now to break the mold  i really need to do something different  but muniz struggled to navigate this  phase in his career  after becoming so well known for his  past characters that he wasn't taken  seriously in other roles for instance in  2007  he switched gears with a role in the  rom-com  my sexiest year which received middling  reviews  and in 2008 he appeared in extreme movie  which was panned by critics  eventually muniz decided to take up a  new passion that surprised some of his  fans  in 2001 he drove the pace car in the  toyota 500 and in 2004  he won the toyota pro celebrity race  however he knew that there was no way  he'd be able to balance both  acting and racing in 2006 he decided to  simply go on hiatus from acting for a  while  telling bbc news i want to want to act  and right now i want to race you can't  really juggle both  because if you do you just don't get  enough time in the car  this wasn't an impulsive decision on  muniz's part  he spent plenty of time training to get  behind the wheel  and he impressed his instructors he  competed with jensen motorsport  and his solid performance in pre-season  testing earned  praise from team boss eric jensen muniz  raced for several years  closing out his racing career with  another showing at the toyota pro  celebrity race in 2011.  while racing muniz got into an accident  and became  seriously injured saying on dancing with  the stars  i had a crash and broke my back and  injured my hands and ribs  it took him quite a while to recover and  he still feels the effects of these  injuries today  he admitted that he and his dance  partner whitney carson  ended up talking about his injuries all  the time during rehearsals because he  felt like he had  quote the creaky old body of a 71 year  old he didn't let his past injuries hold  him back from pursuing  other exciting opportunities and he  still considers himself an active  athletic person at the age of seven  muniz got his first concussion  while playing soccer and since then he  has suffered eight more  later in life he began dealing with  frightening mini strokes  in fact munich says that he had visited  the emergency room  on at least 15 different occasions  because of these  adverse health events the fact that he  survived his first  mini stroke was nothing if not  miraculous  he realized that something was wrong  while he was riding his motorcycle  and while losing his vision he somehow  made it home to his family  i kind of lost all peripheral vision and  like started feeling like i was losing  my balance and uh  just started feeling really really  uncomfortable to this day  muniz has no clear answers as to why he  has suffered from many strokes  he's always been very focused on living  a healthy lifestyle  telling entertainment weekly i'm 31 i've  never sipped alcohol  i've never touched a drug or taken a  drag of a cigarette  the only thing i felt was stress i'm a  high strung person i just like to always  be moving  i'm not good at relaxing for the most  part munis hasn't endured long-term  complications from experiencing mini  strokes but he has dealt with one  setback  memory loss muniz admits that today he  doesn't remember  much of his time working on malcolm in  the middle but munis says that for the  most part his memory loss doesn't bother  him  although dealing with these health  issues can be difficult he chooses to  stay focused on the positives  his wife paige price even helps them  keep track of things they've done  together by writing them down in a  journal  as muniz told people i only know what  it's like to be me  and if i don't let it bother me i just  try to live the most fulfilling best  life i can  i really try to take advantage of my  time and i've got a lot in my life  muniz has a wide variety of interests in  addition to acting  and racing he's also passionate about  music he began playing the drums when he  was 12  and he always enjoyed it as a hobby and  a momentary reprieve from the spotlight  i'm the drummer you know like no one  looks at the drummer you know what i  mean you look at the front man  sorry man no but nobody weren't nobody  looks at the drummer  in 2012 muniz decided to put his racing  career on hold  in order to pursue music professionally  he joined the band you hang up as a  drummer when they were unsigned  it all started with a random message  from aaron brown  the band's lead vocalist and guitarist  as muniz told pin live  aaron called and asked if i'd be  interested in jamming with him  since he knew i played drums i was like  i don't want to jam with you guys  i want to be in the band later muniz  went on to play drums with the band  kingsfoil and in 2017 he switched gears  and began  managing the band astro lasso taking  them on tour with we the kings  although munez has taken long stretches  of time away from acting  he never walked away from the industry  throughout the years  since malcolm in the middle ended muniz  has occasionally done  guest spots on tv shows and appeared in  supporting roles in movies  unfortunately for munez most of his  films have not gotten glowing reviews in  2016  he appeared in the family flick another  day in paradise  which told the story of two girls  helping their widowed father  accept their mother's death in 2018  muniz went in a new direction when he  starred in the horror film the black  string  interestingly enough critics weren't  crazy about the film  but muniz's performance did earn some  praise  with critic britney witherspoon writing  elevating this script from a derivative  and simple one is no easy task  but muniz does it effortlessly muniz  moved to arizona because he was ready to  get away from los angeles  telling penn live i always say moving  out of la  and moving to phoenix i feel saved my  life  later muniz settled down in scottsdale  with his partner  paige price whom he married in 2019 the  couple  loved the area's unique charm and old  west vibes  however he says that new developments in  the city have made him a bit concerned  for scottsdale's future  lamenting in an interview with azcentral  it's becoming like a little bit of a  mini la  not that i want to get into an la bash  fest but i moved here because i love  what it has here  i hope it doesn't grow too big where you  lose some of that charm  muniz and price bought outrageous olive  oils and vinegars in scottsdale arizona  and became  small business owners my fiancee and i  were looking to do something together  and we found this little the store in  this brand and we loved it  and we took it over and muniz didn't  simply hire people to run the store for  him  he took a very hands-on approach with a  couple bottling  labeling and sealing everything  themselves as he explained  in an interview with azcentral it's a  lot of work  but it's really rewarding when people  come in and rave about the product  muniz and price were genuinely proud of  the olive oils and other products they  put on the shelves  before selling the shop in 2020 in  september 2020  muniz and price excitedly announced that  they were going to become parents  the couple revealed to their fans that  they would be welcoming a baby boy into  their family  in the announcement muniz said while we  still believe  it's the little moments in between the  big ones that make you feel happiest  nothing quite compares to hearing your  little one's heartbeat  from that moment munis's focus in life  completely shifted  he immediately started suggesting baby  names and wondering what their child's  future would be like  the couple welcomed their son maz on  march  22nd 2021 and now it looks like muniz  will be focused on spending lots of time  with his family  and enjoying fatherhood fans of muniz  will be happy to hear that despite  stepping away from hollywood  he has no intentions of retiring from  acting altogether  early in 2021 muniz had a guest role as  corey harris on the comedic crime drama  the rookie  he's also set to play a deputy in the  western film  hot bath and a stiff drink too and has a  role in  road to capri a comedy film about two  brothers who only discover that they're  related after their father's death  while muniz might never commit as much  time to acting as he once did  he'll likely stick around in hollywood  for years to come  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite child stars are coming  soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one  [Music]  you

